  "language": "en",
  "text": "Track 7.2 Bicram! Kim! I have found the person and the invention I want to talk about for the invention seminar! His name is Alfredo Moser and he's from Brazil. At last! Well, hurry up and tell us about him! Okay, well, Alfredo Moser invented the bottle lamp which makes light out of old plastic bottles. This is the best invention ever because the design is so simple and it helps some of the poorest people in the world. And it's also a great achievement because it uses materials that we usually throw away and are a problem for the environment. That does sound quite interesting. Tell us more. The lamp is made by filling a plastic bottle with water and chlorine, you know, the chemical that we use in swimming pools, and then you put it in a sunny place. It takes energy from the sun during the day and at night it lights up so you can use it as a lamp. People who live in places with no electricity can use these bottle lamps. They make it possible for children to do their homework in the evenings and families can spend time together. It's amazing! But surely it must be more complicated than that. You can't make a lamp out of a bottle of water. Yes, you can! Although you do need some sort of battery as well as the bottle and a few other simple things, they are cheap and easy to make. Alfredo Moser's life is remarkable in other ways too. The surprising thing about him is that he never tried to get rich from his invention. He wasn't interested in being an entrepreneur and starting a business. His purpose was to help people. The lamp was a big success all over the world, but he didn't try to make money from it. Okay, that's not a bad story. Do you have any examples of situations in which the lamps are used? Lots of places where many people are poor and electricity is unusually expensive. In the Philippines, India, Bangladesh, Tanzania, Argentina, Fiji, all over the world really. People are even starting to grow food in small indoor farms using light from the bottle lamps.",
